  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Chithranjali vs Prashanth.K.S on 5 August, 2025 Author: N.Nagaresh Bench: N.Nagaresh 2025:Ker:58425 In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr.Justice N.Nagaresh Tuesday, The 5Th Day Of August 2025 / 14Th Sravana, 1947 Wp(C) No. 5656 Of 2025 Petitioner: Chithranjali, Aged 52 Years, D/O Late Ittikunjan, Poothully Lane Ernakulam, Pin - 682018 By Adv.Sri.M.A.Saji Roshan Respondents: 1 Prashanth K.S. S/O Soman, Kozhikkulangara, Muhamma Post, Alappuzha, Pin - 688525 2 E.Rafeek, S/O Esmail, Sherin Manzil, Thathanpally Post, Alappuzha, Pin - 688013 3 Station House Officer, Alappuzha North Police Station Alappuzha, Pin - 688001 4 District Police Chief, Office Of The District Police Chief Alappuzha, Pin - 688001 5 Commissioner Of Police, Marine Drive, Ernakulam Ernakulam District, Pin - 682011 Chithranjali vs Prashanth.K.S on 5 August, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/95217315/ 1 2025:Ker:58425 W.P.(C) No.5656/2025 :2: 6 Commissioner Of Food Safety, Thycaud,Thiruvananthapuram, Thiruvananthapuram District, Pin - 695014 7 Director Forensic Science Laboratory, Vazhuthacaud, Thiruvananthapuram, Pin - 695014 8 Director General Of Police, Vazhuthacaud, Thiruvanathpuram, Pin - 695014",
    "facts": "2. The petitioner called Control Room and police came to the spot. The petitioner also received a SMS KL-01-BT- 7941 with number 6238904390 assigned. An ID 1165266 is numbered. On the same day, the petitioner went to North Police Station and submitted complaint. On 11.12.2024, while the 2025:KER:58425 petitioner was sitting at the Chief Judicial Magistrate Court, Alappuzha, Prashanth came from behind, used obscene language and pulled her gown. Again the petitioner called police at 12.14 pm. The petitioner received an SMS from police with ID 1204994. Police came from North Police Station. By the time police came, the accused escaped. Thereafter, the petitioner told the CJM about the attack. The petitioner is seeking direction to the police to register appropriate crime against Prashanth and Rafeek and give her adequate police protection. Though notice was served on respondents 1 and 2, there is no representation for the respondents when the case was called. 4. The grievance of the petitioner is that respondents 1 and 2 are threatening the petitioner.",
    "arguments": "The petitioner is a practicing lawyer. The petitioner is not in a position 2025:KER:58425 to go even to Courts. The petitioner points out an instance of falling down due to hitting by the bike.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The petitioner is a practicing lawyer. The petitioner is not in a position 2025:KER:58425 to go even to Courts. The petitioner points out an instance of falling down due to hitting by the bike.",
